Backport of the functional part of upstream commit fa510bf3
("fix: Missing backup removal", bit-team/backintime, 2026-09-15, issue #2588),
which landed after the v2.0.0-rc2 tag this package pins.

_remove_old_snapshots_date() compared the unit taken from the profile, a
bitbase.TimeUnit, against Config.DAY/WEEK/YEAR, which are ScheduleMode
members, so no comparison ever matched and every unit fell through to
date(1, 1, 1). Retention never removed a single snapshot.

The cosmetic changes of that commit (line wrapping, debug to info) are left
out on purpose to keep the patch reviewable against the tag.

--- a/common/config.py
+++ b/common/config.py
@@ -2080,19 +2080,21 @@
 
     See issue #1943 for further reading.
     """
-    if unit == Config.DAY:
+    if unit == Config.DAY or unit == bitbase.TimeUnit.DAY:
         date = datetime.date.today()
         date = date - datetime.timedelta(days=value)
         return date
 
-    if unit == Config.WEEK:
+    if unit == Config.WEEK or unit == bitbase.TimeUnit.WEEK:
         date = datetime.date.today()
         # Always beginning (Monday) of the week
         date = date - datetime.timedelta(days=date.weekday() + 7 * value)
         return date
 
-    if unit == Config.YEAR:
+    if unit == Config.YEAR or unit == bitbase.TimeUnit.YEAR:
         date = datetime.date.today()
         return date.replace(day=1, year=date.year - value)
 
+    logger.critical(f'Unknown unit: {unit}')
+
     return datetime.date(1, 1, 1)
